# TLS_MODE=external: your own reverse proxy (Traefik, nginx, Nginx Proxy Manager, Caddy, SWAG) holds the certificate and
# forwards to this container's port 80 (docker-compose.proxy.yml). Plain HTTP only: no certificates, no ACME, no local
# CA, nothing on 443. Any Host name is answered, so a proxy that rewrites Host still works; only containers on the
# proxy's network reach this port. The address range the proxy connects from (UPSTREAM_PROXIES, private networks by
# default in that override) is believed about who the client is.
http:// {
	import site
}
